# CR 121.5: combat damage to a Battle removes defense counters -- the same
# CounterType-specific branch dealPermanentDamage already has for a
# planeswalker's loyalty (combat-attack-a-planeswalker), but a distinct
# `if t.Has(cardtype.Battle)` case, not shared code (combatdamage.go).
# The Siege is the human's own, protected by ai: a battle is attacked by its
# protector's opponents (CombatUtil.getAllPossibleDefenders,
# CombatUtil.java:66-73), so the human attacks the battle it controls. ai,
# the protector, is the defending player and has nothing to block with.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
queue attacktarget 2
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks none
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
